{
  "_doc": ["Level layout for a one-button level. Segments play in order; 'bars' is each one's length (keep the total at the excerpt's bar count),", "then re-run: python tools/chart.py skyhigh", "lap = beats per trip round a ring (smaller = faster: double-time; larger = half-time).  shape: circle | ellipse | square.", "jump: out (default) or in.  rocket: extra rings the ball launches through on entering.  reverse / revEvery: direction flips.", "look: palette, bg (stars | tunnel | grid), eq (bars | wave | burst), optional [from, to] ramps: zoom, rot (turns), tilt, drain, vignette; flip.", "follow: the ONE sound this section's taps follow (arp, kick, snare, lead); gate colour shows it. lead: which measured layer the L lane reads.", "motif / cycle: sections sharing a motif name are one repeating figure, charted identically every time.", "warn: label shown two beats before the section.  teach: banner the first time.  plan: one pattern per bar (vocabulary at the top of tools/chart.py)."],
  "id": "ambush",
